<title>FRANCE: New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Sept 96.</title>
<headline>New York top ex-Paris cargo destination in Sept 96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority,the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top export destination from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports last month, despite a strong decline in traffic on 1995 levels.</p>
<p>September 1996 Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 2,956 tonnes, down 34.7 percent on the same month last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 2,613 tonnes, an increase of 22.2 percent on September 1995.</p>
<p>Hong Kong was ranked third with 2,178 tonnes flown ex-Paris last month, up 17.3 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten ex-Paris air cargo destinations in September 1996 and the percentage change on September 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>    City		Tonnes	     Pct change from</p>
<p>						 a year ago</p>
<p> 1  New York	  2,956 tonnes    -34.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Chicago	   2,613 tonnes    +22.2</p>
<p> 3  Hong Kong	 2,178 tonnes    +17.3</p>
<p> 4  Tokyo	     2,103 tonnes    -14.1</p>
<p> 5  Sao Paulo	 1,283 tonnes    +29.5</p>
<p> 6  Mexico City	 994 tonnes    +22.4</p>
<p> 7  Los Angeles	 934 tonnes    +10.8</p>
<p> 8  Miami		 899 tonnes   +162.3</p>
<p> 9  Dubai		 848 tonnes    -11.7</p>
<p> 10 Montreal	    769 tonnes    +27.9</p>
